            <div xml:id="d551">

                <pb facs="0593" n="489" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg489"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.00 Revolutions/200: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-09-14T16:00:00-04:00">September 14,
                            1932—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:21 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>207. Blanche has resumed the Provisional Presidency and has appointed Lagos
                    Minister of War. The infantry took the military aviation field but Merino and
                    most of his aeroplanes had gone to a commercial landing field north of Santiago.
                    Guns are mounted in the Moneda and neighboring buildings. A state of expectancy
                    prevails.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
